      "math_academy_id": "e-2716",
      "problem": "Given a triangle ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/335d1d0e07d6f4a7f3daaa9458a221cb5eebc714866d6494d310699b5b62d78e.svg), we know that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/0d097e17cb3fe4b7dbb225dcbea036db715b976ee6728b0e5709b55ce9100e51.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/f6ff20d28baf805ac27eb6a7822291c152a9b44e6b0743a1a7fe59635bfb5528.svg) Based on the angles, which type of triangle is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/afa0d0e402ca98fc0a1a940db76dd0e08071e0ad436191b596e0a6fb14e69027.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg) be the measure of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/886c073571c9bd4fcf1515db8eda5f14ad06f8eb1a7b0612410eb48e7e744a2a.svg) Then ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/0f90935af5a2c2117a80eadb5bbd88380726fd68fc830df2d81e3b3b4a99a242.svg)\n\nSince the sum of the interior angles is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/4725d33446084ddb65f6736ea0750a68503811aff88fa69e321dee24002e95e4.svg), we have \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/cad788019a25c5b35243f9b4613b75863be29389a9cc71f0708e3235e3300bf2.svg)\n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/4f435d11ba07ac4cd7b06579abd2b5a29657db4e2b6c3ce097e9f6df0907e6fd.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/a77859d66a33dd7ee085d5eea33781e4aadba4d93f2c5cc99cef1e9a128d3b8e.svg) \n\nSo, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/141e6fbb250a22f9c3e054f7bebb3a7e071a1b108418aa8275aac87fa2027b80.svg) is an obtuse triangle because it has an obtuse angle (![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/d543d4ca81776165911a27bbf1cba5e8265c99a599fa8df4e11bad00e10c4903.svg)).",
